WEBVTT

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.840
Twenty minutes late...

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.900
You must be Inquisitor Cortion.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.230
I'm Amon with the STN-J.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.710
If you'll come with us, we'll show you to your...

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.520
Please, let me carry your luggage.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.750
The air here... is oppressive.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.660
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:50.390
...the instant I look away.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.530
I just kept counting...

00:01:55.430 --> 00:02:00.970
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:08.340
...that I'd vomited up.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:14.280
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:19.390
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:25.250
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.300
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:37.970
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.800
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.870
What about over here?

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.360
Hang on a minute. I'm trying something right now.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.500
Look, I'm telling you that won't work!

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.580
Why don't you do it yourself, then?

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.380
Why should I have to do it?

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.610
Come on, try the next one!

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.310
Fine, fine...

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.350
What is it?

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.750
Oh, it's nothing important.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.220
Go on back to sleep, Miss Karasuma.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.120
You're not looking at some strange website, are you?

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.100
Of course not. We're not the Chief.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.660
I don't know about that...

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.360
Browsing of porn sites during work hours is prohibited.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.000
Inquisitor?

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.410
Yup.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.840
You mean the Inquisitor who's coming today?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.770
Nobody ever tells us anything around here.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.940
So we thought we'd poke around a bit.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:03:59.950
Can't get in?

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.220
That's an Inquisitor for you.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.990
Protection this tough is definitely out of the ordinary.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.620
Which means that this guy is a real bigshot.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.060
But why would somebody that important come here?

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:15.160
For a Witch inquisition, of course. To see if we can use him as a Hunter.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.490
Use WHO?

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:20.840
If you're so curious, why not ask him yourself?

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.770
If I could do that, I wouldn't be going to all this trouble.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.330
Still, this whole thing is a little fishy.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.510
Hey, maybe we can get through using this Witch here as a starting point.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.280
I dunno... It might be impossible.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.780
Inquisition of heresy, huh...?

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.280
Anyway, could you just give it a try?

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.560
You there.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.530
I want you to pull over past the next light.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.730
But St. Sebastian Church is...

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:01.840
Understood.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.480
Is this all right...

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.390
Wait, where are you...

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.180
It's just you here?

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:12.680
What?

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:18.550
Uh, yes, sir. I just got a call from Amon.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.250
From Amon?

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:23.360
He said the Inquisitor had arrived at the church he'll be staying at.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.020
I see.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:29.290
He also said the Inquisitor wanted to begin the inquisition right away,

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:32.930
...so he wants Miss Karasuma and Sakaki to go retrieve the subject.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.700
So, this is the man to be put before the inquisition, then?

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.340
Yes, sir. Our list didn't pick him up at all.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.370
What routes did the Inquisitor use to find this guy?

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:50.740
I hear that they work on completely different operating principles than we do...

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:52.660
Different principles?

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:55.460
Yes, just like those of the Middle Ages.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:59.560
I'm sure that this case is something of that sort.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.520
Michael, forward that man's data to my office.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:07.440
I see, boss...

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:24.080
Up to a point, an Al can determine if a person can really be used as a Hunter,

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:28.750
...but the final decision has to be made by a human.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:30.500
You understand why?

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:31.590
Of course.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:42.270
The only people authorized to make that final decision are the Inquisitors.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:50.650
In other words, a single word from him will determine if you're the Hunter or the prey.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.240
That's why he's considered to be so important.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:55.980
That bothers me.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:03.150
This is the place.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:37.450
I knew you would come.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:45.530
Observe.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.010
This is an Inquisition Machine.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.260
Human beings pay back
money they borrow!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:05.190
We're here from Shinjuku Hello Work.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.990
It's about your application.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.400
What do you want?

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.800
Shirou Masuda?

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.160
T-That's right...

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:17.400
What... What are you people doing?

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.370
I want you to come with us for a bit.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.100
Go where?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.740
Warrant for Inquisition

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:24.840
That's a...

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:28.510
I actually don't believe that these devices are necessary,

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:31.040
...but the people at the Factory don't seem to agree.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.850
During mine, it was just words.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:35.750
Just words?

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.680
I see, that's what they seemed like to you.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:44.860
Do you remember the symbols I gave you when I questioned you?

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:47.530
The eight runes the Hagal...

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.960
The sacred numbers linked to the secret mysteries of the Craft.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:55.600
But that can be forbidden fruit.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:00.280
Through bestowing the power of God,

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:04.180
...the test of temptation separates the lambs into angels and fallen angels by...

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.510
Power of God...? Sig?

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:12.390
At the time, of course, I don't think you truly comprehended the true nature...

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:16.660
...of the fruit of knowledge that I brought about in you.

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:18.060
- But that was...
- They're here.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.330
Let us begin at once, then.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:23.160
Bring him to me.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:24.800
Yes, sir.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.680
They're about to start.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:41.220
I see...

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.310
Can you patch the video feed through to me?

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.350
Here you go.

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:10.780
Two years ago, a corpse that had been brutally crushed...

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:12.540
...was found in the middle of Tokyo.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.750
Because the corpse had been so badly damaged,

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.710
...the police ruled the death accidental.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:23.790
However, the truth lies somewhere else entirely.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.530
What are you implying?

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:28.330
You know.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:31.270
You alone know what that man was crushed by.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.540
I don't know. I don't know anything about that.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.410
The Hagal of the stone axe.

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:44.910
Yes, this is the symbol of evil deeds that you used...

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:50.490
...in accordance with the Gematria of the Sepher Yetzirah, the Book of Creation,

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.250
...to release your own Craft!

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:56.050
What... What the hell are you talking about?

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.800
Destruction, ruin, revenge.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.030
You unleashed the dark desires hidden in the depths of your soul.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:05.500
You're wrong... You're wrong...

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.040
Did you enjoy it?

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:12.370
Did you enjoy watching someone being crushed with the power of your own mind?

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:14.340
You're wrong!

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.040
You're wrong!

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.220
I was only protecting myself!

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:23.180
I just wanted to escape!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.650
To protect yourself?

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.260
That's right!

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.780
That's right... I wanted to get away.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.390
It was to protect yourself that you took a human life?

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.600
Words are such convenient things.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.940
He wasn't human.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.400
He was trying...

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.100
...trying to kill me...

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:47.310
It is all right to kill anything that isn't human?

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:51.780
But was he really trying to kill you?

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:55.110
Not human... Not human...

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.990
If I hadn't, he would have killed me!

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:01.950
Can you honestly say it wasn't simply a case of overactive imagination?

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:06.390
Can you say that you weren't hoping to kill him from the very beginning?

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.030
You're wrong, you're wrong...

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.430
...you're wrong, you're wrong!

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:14.070
But death has always followed close at your heels.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.760
That wasn't me! That was a... That was just an...

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:21.180
You're saying, then, that everything that turns on you is crushed?

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.150
Not human...!

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.450
No! No! No!

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.450
No! I'm not a monster!

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.180
I'm... I'm...

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:31.820
But you pursued the power of God.

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.790
You are a human, yet you desired the power of God!

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.590
You fell slave to heresy!

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.060
Heresy? Are you saying that I'm the Devil's minion?

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:44.130
You have no one to blame but yourself. You fell of your own free will.

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:46.540
My own free will?

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:50.030
Show me your true self! Reveal yourself to me this instant!

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:53.370
The real me...

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:55.910
Heretic?! Monster?! Devil?! Heretic?!

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:58.810
No, I'm not a monster!

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:03.640
My power... My true power...

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:05.710
Don't come out...

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:08.690
No, please don't...

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:09.960
Kill...

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.200
Don't...

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.360
I'm gonna kill him...

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:13.560
No, don't!

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:14.930
No, I will kill him!

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.530
Please, don't!

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:17.660
Just this one!

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:21.230
No! No! STOP IT!

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:38.550
I'll kill you!

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.020
DIE!

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:49.260
Amon!

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:51.830
Stay calm. Just wait.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.590
I didn't want to kill him...

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:21.490
I didn't want to kill anyone...

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:32.270
Thus ends the inquisition.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:34.610
Let's go.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.210
I didn't want to kill anyone...

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.020
But he held up under the inquisition.

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:52.890
That's true, he held up in that room.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:16:00.030
But the latent darkness that exists in his soul was laid bare.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:02.270
The Inquisitor said so himself.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:06.280
There isn't anyone who doesn't have a little darkness in their soul.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.340
That may be true.

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:12.710
But there are those that are a shade of gray, and those that are truly black.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:14.890
But...

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:16.150
Wait. He's coming out.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.620
Michael! Masuda is on the move.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:23.480
Okay. He looks like a dangerous customer, so be careful.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:42.880
That's the fourth place...

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.070
His back must really be to the wall...

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:01.650
Excessive power leads humans to eternal darkness.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.200
It is for this reason that endless patience is required.

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:10.300
Those who awaken to their Craft must endure any treatment.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:14.700
If they wish to live in this world.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:20.580
But in the end, that proves to be impossible.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.710
What should I do, then?

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.460
You should know the answer to that.

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.860
Surrender your will, and leave everything to us.

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:37.330
I didn't ask to have the powers of a Witch.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:40.300
Why do you use those powers, then?

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:43.570
I don't know why, myself.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:56.050
Looks like he hasn't had a decent job in the past two years.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:57.690
For two years?

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.420
Something on your mind?

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:04.620
That was right around the time that he started showing signs of his Craft.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.860
You're kidding...!

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.260
Can you really say it's out of the question?

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:14.730
To deliberately force someone out of society in order to awaken their powers.

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:17.970
I wouldn't put it past Solomon.

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:21.840
To get a new Hunter, they might go that far.

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:23.180
Tools...

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.340
You think I'm wrong?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:28.180
Oh well. If you find out anything, let me know.

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:29.680
Okay.

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:31.750
This is the real world.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.980
If you refuse to look at it, you'll never to be able to live in it.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.700
Here ya go, one order of Japanese soup-spaghetti!

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:45.510
Ramen

00:18:57.010 --> 00:19:00.780
Man, I'm so bummed! My cell phone bill this month was over 20,000 yen!

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:03.950
You're stretching yourself too thin, man.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:06.510
Hey, I wonder if there's a wallet or something lying around?

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:17.030
He shoots, he scores!

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.870
What did I do to you?

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.470
Why are you punks doing this to me?

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.940
Who the hell are you calling "punks"?!

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.270
- Defiant, huh?!
- Don't screw with us!

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:28.650
This isn't good...

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.010
Think about what you've done!

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:33.680
Who...

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:36.020
Who are they to me?

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:37.790
They think they can do this to me?

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:38.850
Who am I?!

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:47.130
Well, well. He's tougher than he looks.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.800
They started it. It isn't my fault.

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:52.500
They did this to me. It's not my fault...!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.200
Ow!

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:57.510
Stop that, put him down!

00:19:57.510 --> 00:19:58.530
You guys, get out of here!

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:01.380
H-Hey, is this for real? What are you doin', man?

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:02.500
Ow!

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:03.500
Hey!

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:08.680
That's enough!

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:13.590
Amon!

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.680
I-Is this guy some kinda freak?!

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:18.150
Freak?

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.070
You're...

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:37.900
Who are you?

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:42.210
Are you gonna try something on me, too?

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:50.330
Is it that much fun to crush people?

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:55.760
A fallen angel...

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.870
What? You, too... You, too?

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:00.030
YOU, TOO?!

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.370
I won't let you do this.

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:10.540
Robin, you didn't have to...

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:29.960
About that stone monument he visited...

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:35.060
Folklore has it that it was consecrated to a martyr who was betrayed by her followers.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:36.930
A martyr?

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:40.140
My guess is that she was probably a Witch.

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:45.740
How is she?

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:47.940
I see.

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:50.120
Does something about Robin worry you?

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:03.830
I will be leaving Japan tonight. I don't think we will meet again.

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:08.340
Because you seem to have finally awakened.

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:10.210
What do you mean?

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:14.230
To the pleasure of using your Craft.

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:16.800
What are you saying?

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:18.980
What are you...

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.450
Inquisitor?

00:22:27.790 --> 00:22:28.850
Robin is what...?

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:44.980
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:47.840
Tell me.

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:59.830
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:09.720
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:14.210
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:19.580
...all those promises...

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:25.980
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:31.780
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:40.560
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
